+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "should have the powers, resources, and interest needed to enact the project you propose.)"
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "list_item",
+          "text": "● Explain why the project you developed is suitable for this client. What research, from"
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "published literature and from your own analyses, supports the selection of your proposed project? Using a data-driven analysis, how will you convince your client that this is a project they should undertake?"
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "list_item",
+          "text": "● What additional powers and resources will your client need to carry out the project?"
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "(Remember to use assumptions, but also ground your work in reality as much as you are able.)"
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "list_item",
+          "text": "● If the project is carried out what will happen? In other words, what will the measurable"
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "impact on illegal wildlife trade be? What analysis did you do to determine this?"
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "list_item",
+          "text": "● How likely is the project to reach the expected goal? Also, based on a contextualized"
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "sensitivity analysis, are there conditions or events that may disproportionately aid or harm the project's ability to reach its goal? While you could limit your approach to illegal wildlife trade, you may also consider illegal wildlife trade as part of a larger complex system. Specifically, you could consider how other global efforts in other domains, e.g., efforts to curtail other forms of trafficking or efforts to reduce climate change coupled with efforts to curtail illegal wildlife trade, may be part of a complex system. This may create synergistic opportunities for unexpected actors in this domain."
+        },
