+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "Glossary"
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "“Boots-on-the-ground” Forward Teams: The idiom “Boots on the ground” indicates personnel that are physically at the location of action. In firefighting, these are teams that are at the front lines of the efforts to control a fire event; they have immediate, critical knowledge of the rapidly changing situation."
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "Budget Request: A budget request is a business letter seeking funds for costs, expenses, and/or operating overhead for a project or department within an organization. An annotated budget request provides a justification or rationale for each requested item."
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "Country Fire Authority (CFA): A volunteer fire service responsible for fire suppression, rescues, and response to other accidents and hazards across most of the state Victoria, Australia"
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "Emergency Operations Center (EOC): The central command and control point for emergency related operations and activities, and for requests for activation and deployment of resources (personnel or equipment). A mobile EOC can be deployed near the site of an emergency."
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "Repeater: An unattended radio transceiver that automatically rebroadcasts a received signal at high power on a nearby frequency (±600kHz (0.6 MHz) for VHF & ±5MHz for UHF) or on an adjacent channel."
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "Situational Awareness: The perception of the current elements of an event, understanding their significance, and extrapolating their status to the near future; In other words, the knowledge and understanding what is going on around you."
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "Surveillance: The systematic collection and analysis of data, and the sharing of those data to others who can act upon that information."
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "Transceiver: A radio that can both transmit and receive."
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "UHF: Ultra High Frequency, radio frequencies from 300 megahertz to 3,000 megahertz."
+        },
+        {
+          "type": "paragraph",
+          "text": "VHF: Very High Frequency, radio frequencies from 30 megahertz to 300 megahertz."
+        },
